id: pm-github-8r7c
title: Keep automated sync and closeout PRs current and dispatch caller checks
description: "GITHUB_TOKEN PR workflows wait for approval; only ci.yml is dispatched, CodeQL is absent, no auto-merge is enabled, and daily release advances the protected base."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T09:26:43.864Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T07:00:19.021Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Dispatch declared caller workflows on the proposal head; refresh behind proposals; request protected squash auto-merge; adversarial executable workflow regressions and npm/Bun release gates pass.
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-17T09:27:20.424Z",codex-agent,"Live audit: all 24 caller CodeQL workflows lack workflow_dispatch. Required codeql is missing on pm-jev, pm-lint, pm-review and pm-swarm bot heads; dispatched CI checks succeed on heads despite parked pull_request runs. All closeout callers explicitly select ci.yml. Preserve override semantics and document one-time trigger/override setup. Refresh against the latest default branch, request protected squash auto-merge, and execute adversarial workflow tests. Keep import-fidelity PR 142 untouched."
  "2026-10-17T09:34:40.209Z",codex-agent,"Regression proof: replacing only both final dispatch/maintenance step bodies with origin/main makes the new bot PR suite fail; fixed suite passes 11/11. Tests perform a real default-branch advance and merge and require both CI and CodeQL to redispatch on the new SHA. Missing CodeQL dispatch is warned; zero dispatchable workflows fails; auto-merge denial is soft; unresolved conversations stay blocked. Maintenance is bounded to two hours, with the next daily run rebuilding afterward. Existing explicit ci.yml overrides require one-time removal or expansion alongside the CodeQL trigger."
  "2026-10-17T09:46:00.517Z",codex-agent,"Read-only follow-up audit: pm-ado PR 32 is also blocked by an unresolved changelog placement review (October delivery under the September package release), tracked separately as pm-github-lfcf. Required conversations are preserved. The new monitor uses the verified owned PR number so same-name fork branches cannot be selected for auto-merge."
  "2026-10-17T10:08:37.108Z",codex-agent,"The full integration gate exposed a real diagnostic regression in the new dispatch helper: Bash ERR traps were not inherited by functions, so dispatch denial exited without the required token diagnostic. Set errtrace for the maintenance step and added fast denial regressions for both workflows. Fixed denial cases pass 2/2; reverting only errtrace fails 2/2. No protection was bypassed, and dispatch failure still exits before auto-merge. Full gates are being rerun with final code."
  "2026-10-17T10:18:08.975Z",codex-agent,"The final PM-run regression suite passes 13/13 with zero skipped tests. Reverting only the maintenance bodies fails 12/13 cases; reverting only Bash error tracing fails both denial cases. All 24 audited callers already permit auto-merge and squash, so repository merge settings need no current change. Caller setup remains the documented CodeQL trigger, explicit CI override, and required-check policy declarations. Full npm/Bun CI-identity retries retain every assertion and threshold."
  "2026-10-17T10:31:30.754Z",codex-agent,"Additional root cause verified in current GitHub documentation: workflow_dispatch job checks are excluded from PR evaluation and cannot satisfy required branch-rule checks, even when green on the head SHA. This explains the REST-versus-PR-checks discrepancy. Implement the documented GitHub App path: optional client ID plus private-key secret, mint a current-repository token only after local gates, use it for publication and refresh to trigger eligible native pull_request runs, and retain default GITHUB_TOKEN with an explicit setup notice. Native protections remain enforced; no copied or synthetic green statuses. App-enabled maintenance must end inside the one-hour token lifetime. Source: https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/how-tos/merge-and-close-pull-requests/troubleshooting-required-status-checks and https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/trigger-a-workflow"
  "2026-10-17T10:58:33.282Z",codex-agent,"Final design adds the documented optional App path because manual head checks are ineligible for PR branch rules. The pinned official token action requests only the caller repository and five explicit permissions (contents/pull-requests/actions write; checks/statuses read), with job-end revocation. Key material is supplied only after caller scripts and local gates. Publication and refresh use the App token to trigger eligible native PR runs; empty config retains GITHUB_TOKEN with a notice, and partial config fails. A forty-minute absolute deadline starts immediately after minting so publication delay counts against token lifetime. App-focused regressions pass 8/8, and the complete focused suite passes 21/21. Rollout follow-up is enriched in existing pm-github-aiok; no caller operations were performed."
  "2026-10-17T11:12:34.627Z",codex-agent,Read-only ancestry audit found pm-ado#32 reported UNKNOWN while its head was two base commits behind. Maintenance now checks compare API behind_by independently of merge-state labels. Added real-Git regressions for BLOCKED plus base advance; both workflow cases pass. No caller workflows were dispatched.
  "2026-10-17T11:14:04.919Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: in an isolated copy, replacing only the ancestry-based refresh condition with merge-state BEHIND makes both masked-base-advance regressions fail (0/2 pass); restoring the compare-ancestry condition passes 2/2 with zero skips. Existing maintenance revert fails 18 of 21 regressions; App credential-pair guard revert fails 2/2; dispatch ERR-inheritance revert fails 2/2. No production workflow was invoked for these proofs."
  "2026-10-17T12:22:22.139Z",codex-agent,"The full gate exposed a stale default-branch integration assertion: publication now re-queries the owned PR to retain its verified number, so the old fixed request count is no longer valid. Preserve the behavioral assertions instead: every request uses the caller base, exactly one PR is created, and the final request verifies the owned PR. Restart full gates after this test correction; no runtime safety check is weakened."
  "2026-10-17T12:27:21.029Z",codex-agent,"Standalone integration reproduction exposed fixture host skew: bare pm initialized scratch trackers using the newer global host, while workflow replay used the repository pin, changing merge attributes and correctly triggering the scope refusal. Resolve the fixture executable from node_modules/.bin so direct runs and npm/CI use the same pinned host. Production scope rules stay unchanged."
  "2026-10-17T12:31:53.874Z",codex-agent,"The pinned-host reproduction reached the actual dispatch guard: positive shared caller fixtures lacked a real ci.yml, which the former unfiltered dispatcher never inspected. Seed a committed pull_request/workflow_dispatch CI file in positive fixtures while keeping the dedicated no-dispatchable-workflow regressions unchanged. The additional owned-PR lookup also requires the property-based request assertions already added. Production safety refusals remain intact."
  "2026-10-17T13:38:34.138Z",codex-agent,"Corrected positive fixtures pass 3/3: caller trunk through real preparation/publication, fork PR isolation, and nested npm project. Full restarted npm suite passes 777/777 with zero failures/skips; coverage aggregation and remaining release gates are still pending. Workflow behavior remains protected; fixture initialization is pinned and positive fixtures now include dispatchable CI."
  "2026-10-17T13:46:22.650Z",codex-agent,"Final behavioral revert receipt against the complete current 23-case file: restoring only the two original workflow implementations in an isolated copy yields 1 pass and 22 failures, zero skips. Fixed implementations pass 23/23 (including under the full 777/777 npm suite). The independent ancestry-only revert fails both masked-base-advance cases; restoring ancestry passes 2/2. Full npm release gate exits 0 with all 13 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100; Bun release gate remains running."
  "2026-10-17T14:16:09.163Z",codex-agent,"Final local gates PASS with isolated CI identity (HOME scratch, global/system Git config disabled): npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0, each 777/777 tests, zero failures/skips, all 13 authored modules at exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Linked pm commands pass 23/23 maintenance plus 3/3 real-workflow positive fixtures. Revert receipts: original workflow implementations fail 22/23; ancestry-only, ERR-inheritance and App-pairing reverts each fail 2/2. Caller audit is read-only; all 24 setup requirements are documented, rollout tracked in pm-github-aiok, changelog-placement finding in pm-github-lfcf. No caller dispatch, merge or release performed; PR 142 remains separate."
  "2026-10-18T04:03:26.253Z",codex-agent,"Round 1: merge origin/main preserving import fidelity, address all five review threads with isolated revert proofs, then run both release gates under isolated CI identity. The review body has no outside-diff or nitpick findings. The merge driver attempted history re-anchoring; restored the existing PR history unchanged and replayed the main-branch rollout note through the pinned CLI instead."
  "2026-10-18T04:06:49.014Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 fixes: both detectors accept quoted on keys, one/four-space children, indented and indentless event sequences while rejecting nested input keys. Both auto-merge functions require the App deadline; GITHUB_TOKEN fallback still dispatches checks without arming a merge. README separates App-free version lookup from no release-time stamping. Revert proofs retain every new test: reverting only both detectors fails 16/16 trigger cases; reverting only both auto-merge guards fails 2/2 fallback cases; reverting only the README sentence fails 1/1 documentation contract. Restored fixes pass the focused 21/21 cases."
  "2026-10-18T04:12:29.407Z",codex-agent,"Merge verification: all existing PR history records remain byte-identical; the main-branch rollout note was appended through the pinned CLI. Discarded this operation’s generated merge-driver receipts after restoring authoritative item/history state; no reconcile or history repair ran. Additional strict health reports extension host version skew (pinned 2026.10.13 versus installed extension SDK 2026.10.17) and pre-existing stale items; history_drift is clean. Dependency pins remain unchanged per queue rules."
  "2026-10-18T04:21:37.815Z",codex-agent,"Local full gates remain running on a heavily loaded host. Add a temporary read-only GitHub validation workflow to execute the exact npm and Bun release:check commands with isolated HOME and Git identity on dedicated runners. Remove it before final delivery; no thresholds, assertions, protection rules or publication behavior change."
  "2026-10-18T04:25:27.134Z",codex-agent,"Final merge audit correction: keep the intact origin/main history as the canonical chain, so the PR diff against main removes no existing record. Replay the branch rollout note and documentation link through the pinned CLI. The prior PR-fork records remain byte-identical in merge parent b6d44a0; no record was re-anchored, repaired or edited. This supersedes the earlier choice of the PR fork as primary. Both main and branch rollout context are preserved."
  "2026-10-18T04:45:15.168Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 release gates PASS at 498fd15aa927b325a4a87a314503b0d1943e187f: npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git identity each pass 841/841, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 14 authored modules. Receipts: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39097266861/job/117586199894 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39097266861/job/117586199798 . Linked pm commands pass; detector/App-guard/README revert proofs remain 16/16, 2/2 and 1/1 failures respectively. All five review threads received post-push replies. Remove the temporary validation workflow; implementation and tests remain identical. The main-based rollout history verifies 8/8 with current-item hash equality. Local duplicate full runs were stopped; full gate receipts are from CI. Leave item in progress and unclaimed for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-18T06:35:25.995Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: verified both unresolved CodeRabbit findings on PR #146. Retry failed PR-state and ancestry reads within the existing monitor bounds; retain fail-closed validation of successful ancestry responses. Add real-shell regressions and behavioral revert proofs. Document the orchestrator-verified no-App action_required approval path. Main attestation compatibility merged before changes; no dependency bump. PR #148 has no CodeRabbit review yet."
  "2026-10-18T06:42:43.566Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs retain all new tests: restoring only the PR-state read assignments fails all 4 PR poll regressions (sync and closeout, transient and persistent); restoring only the ancestry read assignments fails all 4 COMPARE poll regressions. Restoring the fix passes 10/10 focused cases, including 2 invalid-success-response fail-closed controls. No SDK mocks or live GitHub mutations; shell executes real local Git merges and checks redispatch on the new head."
  "2026-10-18T06:44:22.666Z",codex-agent,"Local duplicate release gates were stopped before completion because of shared-host contention; no pass is claimed. Run both exact npm and Bun release commands on isolated-identity GitHub runners using a temporary validation workflow, then remove it and verify final-head CI. Initial linked PM run passed the new 10-case regression and workflow-version suite, while two older commands exceeded their 120-second runner limit; rerun those with a 600-second limit without changing assertions or thresholds."
  "2026-10-18T07:00:15.003Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 final gate receipts: npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass 863/863 each at db37fdb9522627d6de7f7009890a748d7052389a, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, all 14 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100. CI identity uses isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config; lint, duplication, privacy, production audit, package dry run, changelog and attestation checks pass. Receipts: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/39105126247 (npm job 117609196631, Bun job 117609196775). Linked PM retries pass 53/53 maintenance and 3/3 integration cases with a 600-second runner budget; existing workflow-version suite and new focused 10/10 regressions also pass. Independent reverts fail 4/4 PR-read cases and 4/4 ancestry-read cases. Fresh-clone strict health passes. Both review threads received post-push replies and CodeRabbit marked them addressed; no manual thread resolution. Remove the temporary validation workflow; source, tests, docs and pins remain identical. Final-head CI will be recorded in the PR body. No PR merge or package release performed."
